Done. The fix is clean and minimal:

What was broken: The test coupled ## Git Status (works with zero history — just reads index state) to `## Recently Changed Files` (needs ≥2 commits to diff). In CI's shallow clone (1 commit), git status works but git log has nothing to diff, so the assertion always failed.

What changed: Before asserting, we now check git rev-list --count HEAD. If there's only 1 commit (shallow clone), we skip the assertion — the function is correctly returning no results. If there's real history (>1 commit), we keep the assertion to catch regressions.
